 t('NCSP 2013 vs NCSS 2020','<b>NCSP 2013:</b> secure ecosystem, assurance framework, 24x7 mechanisms, NCIIPC, indigenous tech, <b>5 lakh</b> professionals in 5 years, fiscal benefits. <b>Issues:</b> poor implementation, weak critical-infrastructure focus, funding, coordination, civil liberties, only defensive','<b>NCSS 2020 (DSCI, Lt Gen Rajesh Pant):</b> 21 areas; <b>Secure</b> (digitisation, supply chain, CII, payments, states, SMEs) · <b>Strengthen</b> (0.25-1% of budget; 15-20% of IT spend; R&amp;D, drills) · <b>Synergise</b> (cyber insurance, <b>cyber envoys</b>, courts)',w=26),
 sec('INTERNATIONAL AND WAY FORWARD','g'),
 t('International','<b>UN Convention against Cybercrime</b> adopted <b>24 Dec 2024</b> (first binding treaty); <b>Budapest Convention</b> (India, Russia, China critical); AU Convention (2014, in force 2023); Digital Geneva Convention (Brad Smith); <b>Tallinn Manual</b> (non-binding)','Legal issues: silence of states, disagreements (IHL, self-defence, due diligence, countermeasures), <b>attribution</b>, accountability',w=26),
 t('Way forward','<b>Resilience:</b> response plans, roadmap, detection (IDS, SIEM), user education','<b>Institutions:</b> ISOs/CSOs, real-life drills, relay CERT-In advisories, <b>cyber minister</b> (Australia)','<b>Innovation:</b> cyber insurance, <b>zero-trust</b>; mindset: "not if but when"',w=26),
